      ],
      "source": "https://southhoustontx.gov/188/City-History",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first public library opened in 1927, and a dedicated building was erected in 1937 beside the current library park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Houston%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "South Houston’s name simply marks its position south of the larger city of Houston, a nod to the state’s namesake, Sam Houston.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
